/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 81 0 R
/T (The Centre for Climate Change and Sustainability \(3CS\) at Ashoka University was established in 2019 to bring together members of the Ashoka community who share an interest in studying, communicating, and mitigating the impacts of human-induced climate change. In its first six years, the 3CS has established itself as one of Ashoka University's most vibrant, active, and multidisciplinary centres. The Centre's inaugural flagship event, Healing Earth, held in February 2021 in the immediate aftermath of the COVID-19 pandemic, exemplified this vision. It brought together rigorous academic approaches to understanding climate change and its impacts with broader perspectives on sustainability that emphasize ecological health and resilience.)
/E (The Centre for Climate Change and Sustainability \(3CS\) at Ashoka University was established in 2019 to bring together members of the Ashoka community who share an interest in studying, communicating, and mitigating the impacts of human-induced climate change. In its first six years, the 3CS has established itself as one of Ashoka University's most vibrant, active, and multidisciplinary centres. The Centre's inaugural flagship event, Healing Earth, held in February 2021 in the immediate aftermath of the COVID-19 pandemic, exemplified this vision. It brought together rigorous academic approaches to understanding climate change and its impacts with broader perspectives on sustainability that emphasize ecological health and resilience.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
